{"content":[{"c":["PULSE*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["KJV translation of a Hebrew word perhaps better rendered as “vegetable” (",{"href":"?bref=Dan.1.12,16","r":"Dan.1.12,16","rawR":"Dan.1.12,16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Dan.1.12,16","value":"Dan.1.12,16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dn 1:12, 16"},"). Not wishing to defile themselves with the king’s food, Daniel and his friends requested permission to live on a diet of vegetables and water. The Hebrew word translated as “vegetable” literally refers to “things sown” and probably includes any kind of edible seed. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Plants_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Plants_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Plants_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Plants"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Pulse","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Dn 1:12, 16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Dan.1.12,16","rawQueryValue":"Dan.1.12,16","sourceRefExact":"Dan.1.12,16"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"0d999e8be1f90ec69055bfece890daf065da924cc4bfd50ec73ef0db43418422","sourceItemName":"Pulse","sourceItemOrder":311,"sourceMember":"Articles/P.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Pulse","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Pulse*","title":"Pulse*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}